body:
@matchai In general the changes LGTM. The main issue I see with the general approach in the PR is that independent styling of vcs segments is no longer possible (e.g. moving just branch names into `right_format`).

If the changes to the root format string are reverted, I feel like this could also be merged without having to consider it as a breaking change to allow for more experimentation prior to an eventual v2 (that said this PR would be another good opportunity to do a v2).

 For a v2-style change any disabled-by-default vcs modules should become enabled-by-default to avoid confusion.

@davidkna I hadn't considered how it would impact the ability to separate modules contained within VCS. That definitely is a configuration trade-off as-is.

As @joshka suggests, the way that `custom` works can be a fix. By default, `$vcs` is in the format string, but it can be broken up and used independently as `${vcs.branch} ${vcs.state}`.

I'm open to keeping vcs disabled-by-default before a v2 release, as we iron this out.
